Build the SG_IO backend against the LikeOS headers.

LikeOS disks are driven the way smartmontools' SG_IO backend expects:
/dev/sdX and /dev/srX answer SG_IO (ATA PASS-THROUGH for the ATA disks
behind them), with the usual device naming, so that backend -- the os_*.cpp
configure selects for such systems -- is the OS backend here as well.  It
takes the __u8 .. __u64 types and the version 4 SCSI generic header from
kernel headers; on LikeOS they come from the port's likeos-smartmontools.h
(the version 3 header and the requests are in the C library's <scsi/sg.h>).

dev_areca.h defines the Areca request codes per system; LikeOS gets the
codes of the SG_IO backend, a copy of that branch.

